WEBVTT

1
00:00:15.724 --> 00:00:18.602
[Superman] <i>Something happened</i>
<i>during the fight.</i>

2
00:00:20.687 --> 00:00:22.814
<i>My powers.</i>

3
00:00:22.898 --> 00:00:26.485
<i>I can't be Superman
for you anymore.</i>

4
00:00:26.568 --> 00:00:30.405
[Jimmy] Clark. Clark.
Hey. Clark.

5
00:00:31.490 --> 00:00:32.658
You okay. man?

6
00:00:33.700 --> 00:00:35.160
Yeah. Yeah.

7
00:00:36.286 --> 00:00:37.606
-Smile.
-[camera shutter clicks]

8
00:00:38.789 --> 00:00:41.917
-Let's get one with you.
-I'm good. Jimmy.

9
00:00:41.959 --> 00:00:44.253
You two are the ones nominated
for an award tonight.

10
00:00:44.336 --> 00:00:45.963
You are nominated too.

11
00:00:47.214 --> 00:00:49.800
Technically.
Superman was nominated.

12
00:00:51.009 --> 00:00:53.345
But it's fine. I'm fine.

13
00:00:54.513 --> 00:00:56.431
[musical horn honking]

14
00:00:56.515 --> 00:00:59.601
[Steve] Good evening.
award co-nominees.

15
00:00:59.685 --> 00:01:01.228
plus Clark.

16
00:01:01.311 --> 00:01:04.147
Which one of you lucky kids
gets to ride up front with me?

17
00:01:04.189 --> 00:01:05.941
[all] Uh...

18
00:01:06.024 --> 00:01:07.150
[chuckles] Just kidding.

19
00:01:07.192 --> 00:01:08.819
The back seat's
for nominees only.

20
00:01:08.860 --> 00:01:10.070
Come on. Kent.

21
00:01:12.364 --> 00:01:14.449
Make yourselves comfortable.
VIPs.

22
00:01:14.533 --> 00:01:17.119
Back there. you've got
all weather floor mats.

23
00:01:17.202 --> 00:01:19.121
adjustable protein shake sleeves

24
00:01:19.204 --> 00:01:21.206
and check this. It's a curtain.

25
00:01:21.290 --> 00:01:24.543
It's like Kent
and I aren't even here.

26
00:01:24.626 --> 00:01:27.045
So you think Superman's
gonna show up tonight?

27
00:01:27.129 --> 00:01:29.881
I'm... I mean. I'm sure
he'll try his best to make it.

28
00:01:29.923 --> 00:01:32.175
I mean. he definitely
wants to be here.

29
00:01:32.217 --> 00:01:35.721
He probably misses the city
as much as it misses him.

30
00:01:36.221 --> 00:01:37.389
Probably.

31
00:01:38.724 --> 00:01:40.976
[Jimmy sighs] Poor Clark.

32
00:01:41.059 --> 00:01:42.644
How long does it usually take
to open up

33
00:01:42.728 --> 00:01:44.563
after your identity's
been shattered?

34
00:01:45.689 --> 00:01:47.691
I'll see if we can talk tonight.

35
00:01:47.733 --> 00:01:49.026
Speaking of tonight.

36
00:01:49.067 --> 00:01:50.652
who's Kara bringing to the gala?

37
00:01:50.736 --> 00:01:53.071
-Oh. you mean like a date?
-Yeah. a date.

38
00:01:53.155 --> 00:01:55.574
She's the most eligible
bachelorette in Metropolis.

39
00:01:55.657 --> 00:01:57.242
I don't think
she's bringing anyone.

40
00:01:57.284 --> 00:01:59.578
She's been full time Supergirl
for the last month and...

41
00:01:59.661 --> 00:02:02.247
Wait! Are you bringing a date?

42
00:02:02.289 --> 00:02:04.124
Well. W.O.R.M.S..
W.O.R.M.S.. W.O.R.M.S..

43
00:02:04.207 --> 00:02:06.084
-reached out to me again.
-Jimmy!

44
00:02:06.126 --> 00:02:07.628
And as a man of business.

45
00:02:07.711 --> 00:02:09.463
I have a contractual obligation

46
00:02:09.546 --> 00:02:12.049
to go on one more date.
uh. tonight.

47
00:02:12.090 --> 00:02:13.592
You're bringing a date to a gala

48
00:02:13.634 --> 00:02:15.302
where Kara is receiving
an award?

49
00:02:15.385 --> 00:02:17.763
Come on. You've seen Kara
on the apps.

50
00:02:17.804 --> 00:02:18.889
She's moved on.

51
00:02:18.930 --> 00:02:20.432
I can't wait until your date

52
00:02:20.474 --> 00:02:23.268
turns you into an octopus
or a human skyscraper or...

53
00:02:23.310 --> 00:02:26.396
Listen. I have this
all under control.

54
00:02:26.438 --> 00:02:28.106
<i>Nothing is gonna happen tonight.</i>

55
00:02:28.190 --> 00:02:29.858
[classical music playing]

56
00:02:29.900 --> 00:02:33.362
You see. Lois.
this is a perfectly normal gala

57
00:02:33.445 --> 00:02:34.655
with perfectly normal...

58
00:02:34.738 --> 00:02:36.281
-[screams]
-[yelps]

59
00:02:36.323 --> 00:02:38.825
The Daily Planet Interns
are being featured tonight.

60
00:02:38.909 --> 00:02:41.411
So Mr. White says
we're your problem now.

61
00:02:41.453 --> 00:02:42.537
What?

62
00:02:43.914 --> 00:02:46.416
-[sighs]
-It's okay. Jimmy. I got this.

63
00:02:46.458 --> 00:02:47.959
-But. Clark...
-It's all right.

64
00:02:48.001 --> 00:02:49.127
It's really okay.

65
00:02:49.211 --> 00:02:50.796
[whispering]
I need something to do.

66
00:02:50.879 --> 00:02:52.255
Wait. I'm gonna go find...

67
00:02:52.297 --> 00:02:53.548
[gala attendees gasping]

68
00:02:53.590 --> 00:02:54.942
[gala attendee whispering]
She's here.

69
00:02:54.966 --> 00:02:56.593
[applauding. cheering]

70
00:03:01.139 --> 00:03:02.224
Kara.

71
00:03:03.141 --> 00:03:04.935
[giggles] She's moved on.

72
00:03:04.976 --> 00:03:06.603
I don't see a date.

73
00:03:06.645 --> 00:03:07.688
Uh...

74
00:03:07.771 --> 00:03:09.147
Hey. Kara!

75
00:03:10.148 --> 00:03:11.858
Over here!

76
00:03:11.942 --> 00:03:14.069
Lois Lane! Jimmy Flamebird!

77
00:03:14.152 --> 00:03:16.071
[vehicle approaching.
tires squealing]

78
00:03:17.155 --> 00:03:18.699
[camera shutter clicking]

79
00:03:28.667 --> 00:03:30.627
Oh. Monsieur Olsen.

80
00:03:30.669 --> 00:03:32.254
<i>Bonsoir. cheri.</i>

81
00:03:32.337 --> 00:03:33.797
[kisses]

82
00:03:33.839 --> 00:03:35.882
Wow! [chuckles] Hello.

83
00:03:35.966 --> 00:03:38.593
You must be
Princess Marina Maru.

84
00:03:38.677 --> 00:03:42.514
Maru. And please. James.
call me Marina.

85
00:03:42.556 --> 00:03:44.349
Cat Grant. Daily Planet.

86
00:03:44.391 --> 00:03:47.561
Is James Olsen
your date tonight?

87
00:03:47.644 --> 00:03:49.855
<i>Oh. oui. bien sur!</i>

88
00:03:51.356 --> 00:03:53.233
Jimmy brought a date.

89
00:03:54.276 --> 00:03:57.821
Jimmy brought a date!

90
00:03:58.905 --> 00:04:01.074
[opening music playing]

91
00:04:22.429 --> 00:04:24.222
That's Jimmy's W.O.R.M.S. date.

92
00:04:24.264 --> 00:04:25.891
Well. Jimmy's always had
a boyish charm.

93
00:04:25.974 --> 00:04:28.393
-[Jimmy chuckling]
-[Lois] Boyish charm.

94
00:04:28.477 --> 00:04:31.730
Anyway. I hope we get a chance
to talk tonight. Clark.

95
00:04:31.772 --> 00:04:33.148
[Flip] The dress is fire.

96
00:04:33.231 --> 00:04:34.876
-[flames billowing]
-[gala attendee screaming]

97
00:04:34.900 --> 00:04:38.028
Uh. sorry. Lois. but I gotta go
get those rascals.

98
00:04:38.069 --> 00:04:39.829
-Come here. you. Come on.
-[cat screeching]

99
00:04:40.739 --> 00:04:42.407
-Lane.
-Vicki.

100
00:04:42.449 --> 00:04:45.202
I can't believe
you turned down a job with me

101
00:04:45.243 --> 00:04:47.621
to stay with
your deadweight boyfriend.

102
00:04:47.704 --> 00:04:49.790
So much promise wasted.

103
00:04:49.873 --> 00:04:53.418
I don't need to work for you
to be a great reporter. Vicki.

104
00:04:53.502 --> 00:04:55.921
And by the way. we're nominated
in the same category.

105
00:04:55.962 --> 00:04:57.714
So I think I'm doing just fine.

106
00:04:57.756 --> 00:05:00.926
You mean co-nominated
with the Olsen kid?

107
00:05:00.967 --> 00:05:02.427
You can't even win an award

108
00:05:02.511 --> 00:05:05.347
without one of your
little boy toys at your side.

109
00:05:05.430 --> 00:05:06.848
[scoffs]

110
00:05:06.932 --> 00:05:08.975
Let's find out what
you're made of. shall we. Lane?

111
00:05:09.059 --> 00:05:12.562
Whoever walks away with
the biggest scoop tonight wins.

112
00:05:12.604 --> 00:05:13.605
Oh. you're on.

113
00:05:13.647 --> 00:05:15.190
You talk a big game. Vicki.

114
00:05:15.273 --> 00:05:17.901
but everyone knows
all that really counts

115
00:05:17.943 --> 00:05:19.528
is what you can do.

116
00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:23.782
[exclaims] Vicki Vale!

117
00:05:23.865 --> 00:05:27.285
Can you believe I used to be
obsessed with her?

118
00:05:27.327 --> 00:05:29.538
Hey. is everything okay?

119
00:05:29.621 --> 00:05:30.789
Oh. yeah. Great.

120
00:05:30.831 --> 00:05:32.040
Everything's great.

121
00:05:43.468 --> 00:05:44.636
[Bizarro] I can help you.

122
00:05:49.474 --> 00:05:51.351
[laughs]

123
00:05:51.434 --> 00:05:53.287
[news anchor] <i>Metropolis has</i>
<i>been missing its hero</i>

124
00:05:53.311 --> 00:05:55.146
<i>for over a month now.</i>

125
00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:58.316
<i>Supergirl is expected to be at
the humanitarian gala tonight</i>

126
00:05:58.400 --> 00:05:59.818
<i>to accept her award.</i>

127
00:05:59.901 --> 00:06:02.404
<i>But will Superman
be there to join her?</i>

128
00:06:02.487 --> 00:06:04.823
Mmm. my friend.

129
00:06:04.906 --> 00:06:06.992
[classical music playing]

130
00:06:12.664 --> 00:06:15.208
Jimmy.
introduce me to your date.

131
00:06:15.292 --> 00:06:19.754
Who you brought to the gala
where I am receiving an award.

132
00:06:19.838 --> 00:06:22.132
[chuckles] Kara. I. uh...

133
00:06:22.173 --> 00:06:23.800
Ah. Supergirl.

134
00:06:23.842 --> 00:06:28.179
You and Superman are greatly
admired even in Markovia.

135
00:06:28.221 --> 00:06:31.182
Metropolis is fortunate
to have you as its guardian.

136
00:06:31.224 --> 00:06:32.601
Thank you. Princess.

137
00:06:32.642 --> 00:06:35.353
But it is Superman
who deserves all the credit.

138
00:06:35.395 --> 00:06:36.730
You deserve the credit.

139
00:06:37.689 --> 00:06:39.357
You saved the city.

140
00:06:39.441 --> 00:06:41.902
And I I know the city's
confusing

141
00:06:41.985 --> 00:06:44.029
and doesn't always know
how it feels.

142
00:06:44.070 --> 00:06:45.447
But everybody in the city

143
00:06:45.488 --> 00:06:48.825
really. really cares
about you. Kara and...

144
00:06:48.867 --> 00:06:50.827
Ah. James Olsen.

145
00:06:50.869 --> 00:06:55.248
You are so kind
to your platonic friend.

146
00:06:55.332 --> 00:06:58.209
[Jimmy] Uh. I mean. I'm...
I'm just. uh...

147
00:06:59.377 --> 00:07:00.837
Good evening and welcome

148
00:07:00.879 --> 00:07:04.382
to Metropolis's 10th Annual
Humanitarian Gala.

149
00:07:04.466 --> 00:07:06.051
[laughing. cheering]

150
00:07:06.092 --> 00:07:08.178
My name is Silver St. Cloud.

151
00:07:08.219 --> 00:07:11.389
And it is my honor
to be your host tonight.

152
00:07:11.431 --> 00:07:15.226
Thank you for joining us here
at the Natural History Museum.

153
00:07:15.268 --> 00:07:17.395
We have an impressive roster
of speakers

154
00:07:17.437 --> 00:07:20.523
<i>and so much charitable service
to recognize tonight.</i>

155
00:07:20.565 --> 00:07:23.610
<i>So please find your seat.
Thank you.</i>

156
00:07:23.693 --> 00:07:25.820
[tense music playing]

157
00:07:31.576 --> 00:07:34.829
Fox to vulture.
Entryway has been secured.

158
00:07:41.002 --> 00:07:42.712
[Clark clears throat]

159
00:07:42.754 --> 00:07:45.507
Uh. Kara. can you believe these
are the bones of a blue whale.

160
00:07:45.590 --> 00:07:47.592
Earth's largest living animal?

161
00:07:47.634 --> 00:07:49.511
Flip. Why don't you tell...

162
00:07:49.594 --> 00:07:50.762
Uh-oh. Flip?

163
00:07:50.804 --> 00:07:53.223
Hey. Clark.
won't you miss Kara's...

164
00:07:53.264 --> 00:07:55.725
Don't worry. I'll be back
before Kara's award.

165
00:07:55.767 --> 00:07:56.810
I promise.

166
00:07:56.893 --> 00:07:57.978
Flip!

167
00:08:00.897 --> 00:08:03.858
[Silver] It's my great
privilege to recognize not one.

168
00:08:03.942 --> 00:08:06.236
but two courageous individuals

169
00:08:06.277 --> 00:08:09.114
who put their lives
on the line for Metropolis

170
00:08:09.155 --> 00:08:11.116
again and again.

171
00:08:11.157 --> 00:08:13.743
Please. a huge round of applause

172
00:08:13.785 --> 00:08:15.870
for Metropolis humanitarians.

173
00:08:15.954 --> 00:08:18.832
-Superman and Supergirl.
-[applauding]

174
00:08:20.834 --> 00:08:22.210
Thank you all.

175
00:08:22.293 --> 00:08:26.172
Kal-El... Superman wishes
he could be here tonight.

176
00:08:27.132 --> 00:08:29.634
but in his absence.

177
00:08:29.676 --> 00:08:32.971
I humbly accept this award
for us both.

178
00:08:33.013 --> 00:08:35.640
I can see why Superman
loves your Earth.

179
00:08:35.682 --> 00:08:38.560
Although I am still new
to this planet.

180
00:08:38.643 --> 00:08:42.063
it is already full
of people I love.

181
00:08:45.692 --> 00:08:49.946
And friends I can count on.

182
00:08:49.988 --> 00:08:53.491
Fox to Vulture. Exits are
locked and alarms are disabled.

183
00:08:53.533 --> 00:08:54.826
Local feed redirected.

184
00:08:54.868 --> 00:08:57.829
Ready to broadcast at your word.

185
00:08:57.871 --> 00:08:59.831
-Princess Maru.
-Vicki. what are you...

186
00:08:59.914 --> 00:09:01.499
You're so outspoken
in your beliefs.

187
00:09:01.583 --> 00:09:04.335
Do you fear public backlash
or even persecution

188
00:09:04.377 --> 00:09:06.921
for your endorsement
of free expression?

189
00:09:07.005 --> 00:09:09.841
[Marina] I have received
several threats. yes.

190
00:09:09.883 --> 00:09:13.678
But I always take
the necessary precautions.

191
00:09:13.720 --> 00:09:16.181
I refuse to be silenced.

192
00:09:18.558 --> 00:09:19.559
Hmm.

193
00:09:19.642 --> 00:09:21.352
Leaving already. Lane?

194
00:09:21.394 --> 00:09:23.938
[whining]
That's what you sound like.

195
00:09:24.898 --> 00:09:28.735
[all laughing]

196
00:09:28.818 --> 00:09:30.111
[grunts]

197
00:09:33.865 --> 00:09:35.700
What's all this?

198
00:09:36.576 --> 00:09:38.161
-[guard groans]
-[gasps]

199
00:09:38.203 --> 00:09:39.329
Who's there?

200
00:09:42.707 --> 00:09:44.876
[gasps]

201
00:09:44.959 --> 00:09:48.630
Uh. I think we need to tell
someone about this.

202
00:09:48.713 --> 00:09:49.881
Like who?

203
00:09:52.759 --> 00:09:53.885
Flip?

204
00:09:54.552 --> 00:09:55.970
Kids?

205
00:09:56.054 --> 00:09:58.139
[groans] Anyone?

206
00:09:58.181 --> 00:10:02.393
Be really great to have
super-hearing right about now.

207
00:10:02.435 --> 00:10:08.650
[disembodied voices
whispering indistinctly]

208
00:10:09.734 --> 00:10:11.111
Flip?

209
00:10:11.194 --> 00:10:14.239
Um. stop being creepy.

210
00:10:25.208 --> 00:10:26.459
What in the...

211
00:10:26.543 --> 00:10:30.463
[disembodied voices
whispering indistinctly]

212
00:10:31.631 --> 00:10:36.761
[disembodied voices
speaking indistinctly]

213
00:10:36.845 --> 00:10:38.555
[Flip screaming]

214
00:10:39.180 --> 00:10:40.431
Flip!

215
00:10:40.515 --> 00:10:41.992
[Lois] So you have absolutely
no opinions

216
00:10:42.016 --> 00:10:44.561
on the growing armed
presence here tonight?

217
00:10:44.602 --> 00:10:46.229
Do you have thoughts
on anything?

218
00:10:47.981 --> 00:10:50.525
Fine. Who's in charge here?

219
00:10:50.608 --> 00:10:51.985
[Silver] That would be me.

220
00:10:52.944 --> 00:10:55.280
Oh. hi. Silver. [chuckles]

221
00:10:55.363 --> 00:10:58.449
I... I just wanted to...
Have you seen...

222
00:10:58.533 --> 00:11:00.743
I'm a big fan
of your work. Lois.

223
00:11:00.785 --> 00:11:03.037
You're a terrific reporter.

224
00:11:03.121 --> 00:11:05.915
Oh. wow. Thank you.

225
00:11:05.957 --> 00:11:09.460
But these interrogations are
kind of bringing down the vibe.

226
00:11:09.502 --> 00:11:11.004
You know what I mean?

227
00:11:11.087 --> 00:11:13.423
The added security is
Princess Maru's private detail.

228
00:11:13.464 --> 00:11:14.883
That's all.

229
00:11:14.966 --> 00:11:16.050
I'm sorry. Silver.

230
00:11:16.134 --> 00:11:17.969
I'm just in this
stupid competition

231
00:11:18.011 --> 00:11:19.262
with Vicki tonight and...

232
00:11:19.304 --> 00:11:21.306
Tonight's awards
aren't enough for you two?

233
00:11:21.347 --> 00:11:22.891
Okay. I guess I'm always in

234
00:11:22.974 --> 00:11:24.934
a stupid competition with Vicky.

235
00:11:24.976 --> 00:11:27.437
but. I mean. what's enough?

236
00:11:27.478 --> 00:11:28.855
I don't know.

237
00:11:28.938 --> 00:11:30.857
But I do know
that if you need an award

238
00:11:30.940 --> 00:11:32.400
to tell you that you're enough.

239
00:11:32.483 --> 00:11:34.986
-you'll never get there.
-[groans]

240
00:11:35.028 --> 00:11:36.321
Just do your best.

241
00:11:36.362 --> 00:11:38.656
And if you can celebrate
whatever that brings you

242
00:11:38.698 --> 00:11:40.158
with the people you love.

243
00:11:40.200 --> 00:11:42.285
well. that's as much
as anybody gets.

244
00:11:44.746 --> 00:11:47.248
Wait. Where are
the people I love?

245
00:11:48.499 --> 00:11:50.668
[dramatic music playing]

246
00:11:55.173 --> 00:11:56.591
Get away from them!

247
00:11:59.385 --> 00:12:00.511
My powers.

248
00:12:16.903 --> 00:12:19.239
Is everyone all right?
Anybody hurt?

249
00:12:19.322 --> 00:12:20.782
You're hurt. Clark.

250
00:12:21.658 --> 00:12:22.992
Where's Superman?

251
00:12:23.034 --> 00:12:25.703
I... I'm sorry. I...

252
00:12:27.205 --> 00:12:28.581
[door opens]

253
00:12:28.665 --> 00:12:30.917
-Come on. We have to go now.
-[soldier] Hey. you!

254
00:12:34.170 --> 00:12:35.546
Clark?

255
00:12:35.588 --> 00:12:36.714
Anyone?

256
00:12:38.049 --> 00:12:40.551
This is Vulture.
I got another stray.

257
00:12:40.593 --> 00:12:41.761
[screams]

258
00:12:48.559 --> 00:12:50.728
-Shh.
-Clark. there's a man.

259
00:12:50.812 --> 00:12:52.939
Yeah. His friend just shot me.

260
00:12:53.564 --> 00:12:54.607
[gasps]

261
00:12:55.900 --> 00:12:57.318
[grunts]

262
00:12:59.112 --> 00:13:01.239
[grunts] Vulture to Fox.

263
00:13:01.322 --> 00:13:04.033
I have strays in the hallway.
I'll take care of them.

264
00:13:04.075 --> 00:13:06.077
Confirm when you have hands
on the princess.

265
00:13:06.119 --> 00:13:08.538
Hands on the princess?

266
00:13:08.579 --> 00:13:11.332
And now please join me
in welcoming

267
00:13:11.416 --> 00:13:13.751
our esteemed keynote speaker.

268
00:13:13.793 --> 00:13:15.253
Her Royal Highness.

269
00:13:15.295 --> 00:13:18.715
Princess Marina Maru
of Markovia.

270
00:13:18.756 --> 00:13:20.967
[applauding. cheering]

271
00:13:22.468 --> 00:13:23.678
Kara.

272
00:13:23.761 --> 00:13:25.555
<i>Jimmy. Princess Maru
has a problem.</i>

273
00:13:25.596 --> 00:13:27.932
Armed men have broken in
and they're after her.

274
00:13:29.976 --> 00:13:33.021
I am Princess Marina Maru.

275
00:13:34.230 --> 00:13:36.190
But you may call me...

276
00:13:37.483 --> 00:13:39.277
Dr. Poison!

277
00:13:39.319 --> 00:13:40.820
[crowd gasping]

278
00:13:40.903 --> 00:13:43.406
[Dr. Poison] I am here to
reverse the Anthropocene era.

279
00:13:43.448 --> 00:13:48.244
curing our Mother Earth
of the disease of humankind!

280
00:13:48.286 --> 00:13:50.288
-[Lois] <i>Jimmy!</i>
-I guess I have a type.

281
00:13:50.371 --> 00:13:53.750
And what better place
to start this revolution

282
00:13:53.791 --> 00:13:57.462
than here at the mausoleum
you've created

283
00:13:57.503 --> 00:13:59.714
for the animals of Le Monde.

284
00:13:59.756 --> 00:14:04.886
Prepare to leave on four legs
or not at all!

285
00:14:09.682 --> 00:14:10.975
[roars]

286
00:14:11.809 --> 00:14:13.811
[screams]

287
00:14:13.853 --> 00:14:16.022
-[crowd screaming]
-[animals screeching]

288
00:14:21.152 --> 00:14:23.154
You! Stop!

289
00:14:24.489 --> 00:14:26.157
Ah. Supergirl.

290
00:14:26.199 --> 00:14:29.160
Such a pity my poison
does not work on you.

291
00:14:29.202 --> 00:14:31.871
but you have other problems. no?

292
00:14:31.954 --> 00:14:33.373
At this very moment.

293
00:14:33.456 --> 00:14:35.958
my henchmen are
at the Metropolis Dam.

294
00:14:36.000 --> 00:14:37.919
Ready to release my poison

295
00:14:38.002 --> 00:14:41.714
directly into the city's
water supply.

296
00:14:41.798 --> 00:14:45.093
Can you be
in two places at once?

297
00:14:45.176 --> 00:14:46.594
Kara. go save the city.

298
00:14:46.636 --> 00:14:50.264
Dr. Poison is
my contractual obligation.

299
00:14:51.516 --> 00:14:52.683
[grunts]

300
00:14:56.771 --> 00:14:58.648
[soldier grunting]

301
00:14:59.190 --> 00:15:00.441
Open up!

302
00:15:00.525 --> 00:15:03.403
Uh. how are you gonna stop him?

303
00:15:06.364 --> 00:15:07.365
I...

304
00:15:07.448 --> 00:15:08.574
[Lois] Wait.

305
00:15:09.033 --> 00:15:10.576
[grunts]

306
00:15:14.247 --> 00:15:16.290
[gas hissing]

307
00:15:17.542 --> 00:15:18.751
[coughing]

308
00:15:19.419 --> 00:15:21.254
[screeching]

309
00:15:24.424 --> 00:15:26.926
Any ideas on how to stop
Dr. Poison?

310
00:15:27.009 --> 00:15:29.303
<i>-Uh...
-She's your date.</i>

311
00:15:29.345 --> 00:15:32.807
<i>Wait. Your boyish charm.
Use your boyish charm!</i>

312
00:15:32.890 --> 00:15:34.642
<i>I... I don't think
it works like that.</i>

313
00:15:38.062 --> 00:15:39.856
Oh. no. No. no. no.

314
00:15:39.897 --> 00:15:42.400
I don't want to be a wolf again.

315
00:15:43.234 --> 00:15:45.319
Uh. what?

316
00:15:45.403 --> 00:15:47.530
This way. kids.
We're almost there.

317
00:15:48.489 --> 00:15:49.824
[growling]

318
00:15:51.409 --> 00:15:52.410
It's over!

319
00:15:52.493 --> 00:15:53.911
The guard.

320
00:15:53.995 --> 00:15:55.580
I thought his name was Vulture.

321
00:15:55.663 --> 00:15:57.582
Back up. kids! Back up!

322
00:15:58.291 --> 00:16:00.001
[roars]

323
00:16:00.084 --> 00:16:02.211
[Dr. Poison] Get to the chopper!

324
00:16:02.253 --> 00:16:03.379
[Jimmy] Wait!

325
00:16:03.421 --> 00:16:04.755
Princess Maru!

326
00:16:04.797 --> 00:16:05.882
James?

327
00:16:08.092 --> 00:16:11.053
Princess. please listen to me.

328
00:16:12.346 --> 00:16:14.515
[Dr. Poison]
This form suits you. James.

329
00:16:14.599 --> 00:16:17.393
But sadly. this must be <i>adieu.</i>

330
00:16:17.435 --> 00:16:19.854
But didn't you feel
our connection?

331
00:16:19.937 --> 00:16:22.482
Our animal attraction?

332
00:16:22.982 --> 00:16:25.776
I... Well...

333
00:16:25.818 --> 00:16:27.862
[dramatic music playing]

334
00:16:27.945 --> 00:16:30.114
[crocodile hissing]

335
00:16:35.328 --> 00:16:37.205
Everyone. keep going.

336
00:16:37.288 --> 00:16:38.956
Lois. what are you...

337
00:16:41.459 --> 00:16:42.502
Lois?

338
00:16:42.585 --> 00:16:43.794
[grunts]

339
00:16:46.130 --> 00:16:47.215
Lois!

340
00:16:55.806 --> 00:16:57.058
[screams]

341
00:16:58.351 --> 00:16:59.435
Lois!

342
00:17:02.396 --> 00:17:03.523
[cat meows]

343
00:17:04.524 --> 00:17:05.566
Are you...

344
00:17:05.608 --> 00:17:07.318
Up here. Smallville.

345
00:17:07.360 --> 00:17:08.444
Cat?

346
00:17:09.362 --> 00:17:11.030
Yeah. yeah. yeah. Keep going.

347
00:17:12.490 --> 00:17:15.493
James. you beautiful fool.

348
00:17:15.576 --> 00:17:19.997
You were just a pawn
in my world-altering game.

349
00:17:20.081 --> 00:17:24.210
A handsome pawn. <i>oui.</i>
but a pawn <i>seulement.</i>

350
00:17:24.293 --> 00:17:25.920
I'm sorry. What was that?

351
00:17:25.962 --> 00:17:30.174
I can't understand you
because of your gas mask.

352
00:17:30.216 --> 00:17:32.468
Do not think me cruel. James.

353
00:17:32.510 --> 00:17:34.804
But I only arranged
a date with you

354
00:17:34.845 --> 00:17:38.015
to gain access to this event.

355
00:17:38.057 --> 00:17:41.644
But now I must shed you
like so much snakeskin.

356
00:17:41.686 --> 00:17:43.312
But wait.

357
00:17:43.354 --> 00:17:44.564
Just one more thing.

358
00:17:45.565 --> 00:17:46.816
[roars]

359
00:17:46.857 --> 00:17:49.026
[screams]

360
00:17:50.861 --> 00:17:53.573
[bones cracking]

361
00:17:58.369 --> 00:18:00.830
That's enough!

362
00:18:02.623 --> 00:18:03.874
[coughing]

363
00:18:03.916 --> 00:18:05.209
Shark to Fox.

364
00:18:05.293 --> 00:18:08.004
Operation Make a Splash
has been compromised.

365
00:18:15.261 --> 00:18:17.805
<i>Allons-y. Maintenant!</i>

366
00:18:19.890 --> 00:18:21.726
Bad dog.

367
00:18:24.395 --> 00:18:25.938
[gunfire]

368
00:18:34.947 --> 00:18:36.073
[explosion]

369
00:18:41.245 --> 00:18:42.288
[barks]

370
00:18:42.371 --> 00:18:44.915
Huh? Who...

371
00:18:46.417 --> 00:18:48.419
[animals screeching]

372
00:18:56.260 --> 00:19:01.432
James. I am so sorry to have
broken your fragile heart.

373
00:19:01.474 --> 00:19:03.392
Don't worry. you didn't.

374
00:19:03.434 --> 00:19:05.102
There are more sharks
in the sea.

375
00:19:05.186 --> 00:19:08.439
my delicious pound cake.

376
00:19:08.481 --> 00:19:10.900
You will forget
our restless rendezvous

377
00:19:10.941 --> 00:19:15.363
and someday find true love.

378
00:19:15.404 --> 00:19:17.448
I'm already in love
with someone.

379
00:19:17.490 --> 00:19:20.576
I've just been really.
really stupid about it.

380
00:19:20.618 --> 00:19:22.411
Of course. <i>c'est moi.</i>

381
00:19:22.453 --> 00:19:23.621
Her name is Kara.

382
00:19:25.581 --> 00:19:29.251
[scoffs] Whatever makes
you feel better. James.

383
00:19:29.293 --> 00:19:30.961
<i>Au revoir!</i>

384
00:19:31.003 --> 00:19:32.129
[sighs]

385
00:19:36.175 --> 00:19:37.343
[meows]

386
00:19:38.594 --> 00:19:41.097
[gasps] Silver. Hi.

387
00:19:41.138 --> 00:19:44.183
Lois. I wanted
to congratulate you

388
00:19:44.266 --> 00:19:46.477
on your award.

389
00:19:46.519 --> 00:19:49.689
[gasps] I won? [gasps]

390
00:19:50.815 --> 00:19:54.026
I mean. thanks. Silver.

391
00:19:54.110 --> 00:19:56.987
[chuckles] Enjoy the rest
of your night. Miss Lane.

392
00:19:57.029 --> 00:20:02.410
Well. obviously. the work
itself is its own reward.

393
00:20:02.493 --> 00:20:05.162
Here. Flip. Do you want this?

394
00:20:05.246 --> 00:20:06.872
-Uh. thanks.
-[Vicki groans]

395
00:20:09.417 --> 00:20:12.753
Okay. she's gone. Give it back.
Ooh! It's so shiny!

396
00:20:19.009 --> 00:20:20.678
-Jimmy Flamebird!
-[Jimmy screams]

397
00:20:20.761 --> 00:20:22.972
Why did you share feelings
with Dr. Poison

398
00:20:23.013 --> 00:20:25.182
that you would not
share with me?

399
00:20:25.224 --> 00:20:27.768
I thought it seemed
like you moved on.

400
00:20:27.810 --> 00:20:30.771
You were on the apps.
You... You'd been dating people?

401
00:20:30.855 --> 00:20:33.816
No. I wanted to be together.

402
00:20:33.858 --> 00:20:37.361
You ran away and and played
your stupid Earth games.

403
00:20:37.403 --> 00:20:39.155
Then Kal-El became distant.

404
00:20:39.196 --> 00:20:43.409
And... And you stopped
talking to me.

405
00:20:43.492 --> 00:20:47.288
I... I thought you just
wanted to be friends.

406
00:20:47.371 --> 00:20:48.914
How can you be my friend

407
00:20:48.998 --> 00:20:51.625
if you hide
when I need you most?

408
00:20:53.502 --> 00:20:56.005
I'm sorry. Kara.

409
00:20:56.046 --> 00:20:57.965
I didn't understand
how you felt.

410
00:21:00.301 --> 00:21:01.677
You did not ask.

411
00:21:07.099 --> 00:21:09.894
Clark. we did it!
We saved the city.

412
00:21:09.935 --> 00:21:11.353
Jimmy and I won the award.

413
00:21:11.395 --> 00:21:15.065
-And you...
-I didn't do anything. Lois.

414
00:21:15.107 --> 00:21:18.360
You saved the kids.
Jimmy defeated Dr. Poison.

415
00:21:18.402 --> 00:21:19.862
Kara saved the city.

416
00:21:19.904 --> 00:21:22.323
All I did was get shot
and locked in a closet.

417
00:21:22.406 --> 00:21:23.908
Metropolis needed a hero.

418
00:21:23.949 --> 00:21:27.369
and all I could give them
was Clark Kent.

419
00:21:28.579 --> 00:21:31.791
Hey. I love Clark Kent.

420
00:21:31.874 --> 00:21:34.794
Well. he's no Superman.

421
00:21:34.877 --> 00:21:38.047
Clark. you can't spend
the rest of your life

422
00:21:38.088 --> 00:21:41.467
comparing yourself to someone
you might never be again.

423
00:21:41.550 --> 00:21:43.260
And what am I supposed to do?

424
00:21:45.137 --> 00:21:46.806
Who am I supposed to be?

425
00:21:51.268 --> 00:21:52.520
[screams]

426
00:21:52.603 --> 00:21:53.646
[screams]

427
00:21:54.605 --> 00:21:55.606
Huh?

428
00:21:55.648 --> 00:21:56.857
[both scream]

429
00:22:04.323 --> 00:22:05.741
[theme music playing]
